The package has no go.mod of its own, so it belongs to the
github.com/hashicorp/vault module, whose repository LICENSE is BUSL-1.1
even though these particular files are MPL-2.0. Importing the package as a
module would therefore place a BUSL-1.1 module in go.mod for the sake of
two MPL-2.0 files. Copying them keeps the license position unambiguous.
internal/shamir/UPSTREAM records the commit the copy came from, and CI
fails if the copy drifts from upstream.

